# Patch: keep webui-init validation offline so the panel cannot freeze
#
# Upstream: Enginex0/tricky-addon-enhanced @ v5.53.1 (5c5e497)
# Applies to: rust/src/keybox/validate.rs, rust/src/cli/webui_init.rs
#
# validate_full() fetches Google's attestation status
# (https://android.googleapis.com/attestation/status) for the revocation
# list. On blocked/unreachable networks that request stalls for a long time
# (DNS and connect hangs), and the KernelSU-style WebUI bridge executes
# commands synchronously in the @JavascriptInterface method - one stalled
# fetch freezes the whole WebUI page (the app-list spinner never clears)
# and the Enhanced panel stays on its loading placeholder forever. The
# per-process CLI has no revocation cache, so every panel open / startup
# preload triggered the fetch again.
#
# This patch splits validation into an online path (still used for user
# initiated keybox fetching/custom installs, where the network is expected)
# and an offline path that uses only the embedded revocation list.
# webui-init now uses the offline path: the panel opens instantly and never
# touches the network.
#
